ry. But then Superman goes back to Metropolis and suddenly they're super important to the story again.<br /> <br /> So how does a VtM game work? Like a solo act, or like a team?<br /> <br /> Well, V5 even more so than any edition? It's a team. The coterie is much more strongly built into the game as it's own entity (things like the Relationship Map). Campaign Tenets reinforce that this is the story of a group of main characters, not a main character and a bunch of satellite characters. I'll add your love of Bloodlines is a great example here... Bloodlines is a solo act, and unsurprisingly it's easier for Bloodlines to have more mortal NPCs that matter and are interesting.<br /> <br /> So no, it really shouldn't be surprising that people balk at V5 also trying to wedge humans into the forefront.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>This is really unfair. V5 is demanding that you write up a Jimmy, Lois, and Perry for all of your characters. Being annoyed that you have to go this route (at least to have Convictions) isn't a statement of one game being better or worse than another. It's a statement of the game not supporting both equally.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think the PG also need to address the &quot;one Touchstone to one Conviction,&quot; issue for this to really work out. One of the reasons Touchstones work in Requiem is they're all attached equally to Humanity as a whole. Why a Touchstone matters is because they matter to your character in a meaningful way to support the broad idea of Humanity. V5 insisting that each Touchstone being linked to a specific ideal/belief/etc.gives an off-putting and ill-fitting forced narrative on them; esp since V5 doesn't let you regain Touchstones if you lose them (opposed to when you can transition from one to the other).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, exactly, especially the bolded part.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T06:11:30-07:00","id":1333517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1333289#post1333289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">,long, detailed description of how Touchstones work in V:R2&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>That you, I will now use this instead of the V5 bodgejob, if I ever need to.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T13:41:19-07:00","id":1333588,"title":"","content":"If you're interested in adapting a more Requiem approach to Touchstones to VtM (whichever edition), we should probably start a new thread. While the broad strokes stuff I detailed are useful for the specific issue of V5's defining of what a Touchstone can be, there is a broader mechanical context to consider if actually porting things over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T20:08:49-07:00","id":1333632,"title":"","content":"Time for some tin-foil!<br /> <br /> The Tremere have been going on around a thousand years and they're still the most hatred Clan in the Kindred world. With the schenanigans going on with folks directing mortal intelligence and military forces against their enemies, sooner or later someone was going to decide to just start dropping hints about every Tremere they could in the laps of the CIA or the GRU. The Tremere asked themselves &quot;what's harder than killing us all when we're part of one Sect?&quot; and then decided to make their play.<br /> <br /> They cleared out everything legit from the Prime Chantry and left only occult mock-ups and the more disposable folks, then anonymous dropped enough details to various members of other Clans who would have loved to kill off the Tremere and let them go to work running to the SI. Now they're just waiting for a few more years to pass, at which point they'll be firmly entrenched across three Sects and can then start exposing/&quot;exposing&quot; all the folks who you see in the Anarch and Camarilla books talking about how their Clans were behind the Prime Chantry attack. &quot;They were talking about their Clan colluding with the SI a few years back. Go on. Ask them. Then make some calls, cause I'm sure the Inner Circle would love to hear about this.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25611-gilbythefat","name":"GilbyTheFat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25611_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-04T10:22:44-07:00","id":1333981,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.economist.com/graphic-detail/2019/09/04/vienna-remains-the-worlds-most-liveable-city?fsrc=scn/tw/te/bl/ed/viennaremainstheworldsmostliveablecitydailychart\" target=\"_blank\">Vienna remains the world\u2019s most liveable city</a></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the Economist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the EIU\u2019s index, which ranks 140 cities on 30 factors bunched into five categories\u2014stability, health care, culture and environment, education and infrastructure\u2014Vienna scores a near-perfect 99.1 out of 100, putting it just ahead of Melbourne.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this ranking is only possible because of the fall of the main Tremere chantry. </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-04T12:42:38-07:00","id":1334004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1333981#post1333981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.economist.com/graphic-detail/2019/09/04/vienna-remains-the-worlds-most-liveable-city?fsrc=scn/tw/te/bl/ed/viennaremainstheworldsmostliveablecitydailychart\" target=\"_blank\">Vienna remains the world\u2019s most liveable city</a></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> <br /> And this ranking is only possible because of the fall of the main Tremere chantry. </span></div> </div> </div> </div>The SI is doing good work! Look how much of an improvement this is!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-04T13:37:14-07:00","id":1334016,"title":"","content":"<i>Looks at how much of an improvement that actually was</i><br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure we mean this ranking is only possible because the SI is rigging the survey to cover up the attack on the Tremere Chantry.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-04T15:23:53-07:00","id":1334028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1334016#post1334016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">..the SI is rigging the survey to cover up the attack on the Tremere Chantry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pft. As if. The Tremere were bleeding the city dry, they were sucking the life blood out of Vienna. The quality of life has gone up a lot when the city is no longer home to life-eating monsters. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-04T17:20:54-07:00","id":1334037,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure that Vienna placing near or in the top ten for all the years of the current liveability methodologies means the Tremere weren't doing much bleeding dry. Every year after the fall of the Chantry them getting #1 (even though a terror attack should have knocked them down for a year or two) is much more suspicious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T18:19:44-07:00","id":1400870,"title":"","content":"I have a fitting question. It is said that there is now a prohibition for any member of the clan to move to Vienna? But what about any of those that lived there and managed to survive? In my chronic there is a jewish who whas embraced during the &quot;Reichskristallnacht&quot; and got later as a reward to be able to build there own small haven somewhere in Vienna outside the chantry where she where during the event. Now how should I handle her?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T19:21:22-07:00","id":1400880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1400870#post1400870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a fitting question. It is said that there is now a prohibition for any member of the clan to move to Vienna? But what about any of those that lived there and managed to survive? In my chronic there is a jewish who whas embraced during the &quot;Reichskristallnacht&quot; and got later as a reward to be able to build there own small haven somewhere in Vienna outside the chantry where she where during the event. Now how should I handle her?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that you can do whatever works best for your campaign, though I'm inclined to think that they should be worried about the fact the Second Inquisition are everywhere there now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1334037#post1334037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure that Vienna placing near or in the top ten for all the years of the current liveability methodologies means the Tremere weren't doing much bleeding dry. Every year after the fall of the Chantry them getting #1 (even though a terror attack should have knocked them down for a year or two) is much more suspicious.</div> </div> </div> </div>The World of Darkness is not our world, I point out for the fact Montreal is a Satanism filled hellhole with one of the highest murder rates in the world.<br /> <br /> O'Tolleys also replaces Applebees and thus the food quality is slightly better.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T06:42:08-07:00","id":1400950,"title":"","content":"My take on the Vienna incident is the early Second Inquisition was acting with the full support of the Technocracy, a support that progressively weakened after the destruction of the prime chantry BECAUSE they thought that destroying &quot;Vampire Central&quot; meant the rest of the &quot;ematovores&quot; were now easy pickings and left the Second Inquisition to deal with them alone or with minimal support (their resources were better spent trying to gain control of Reality, which is the Technocracy's goal after all). This was of course a wrong assumption, but one that benefitted several parties.<br /> <br /> Some elements from older books that could support this theory:<br /> <br /> -The Technocracy was always aware of vampires but never considered hunting them down a top priority (among &quot;reality deviants&quot; thay are extremely well behaved since they enforce their own masquerade) this UNTIL the week of nightmares. The Technocracy had to authorize Operation Ragnar\u00f6k with orbital concentrated sunlight and spirit nukes involved. In the end they managed to destroy the Ravnos antediluvian but at a great cost in terms of their resources.<br /> -From this incident the Technocracy learned of the potential threat to the Consensus posed by vampires. They did not know the full picture, what an Antediluvian was and how rare occurrences such as the week of nightmares actually were. All they knew was the damage that had been wrecked and the cost they had to pay to contain the breach. Suddenly getting rid of vampires became a priority.<br /> -Other agencies noticed what happened, Vampires included. Those in the known about the Antediluvian's existence realized one of their number had been destroyed... and it was the result of humanity's actions. One of the Vampires who took notice of Ravnos' destruction was Tremere, who had recently been forced to flee his own body in order to avoid finally being consumed by Saulot. Now inhabiting Goratrix's body, Tremere had enacted a ritual to kill all of the antitribu and get back to 3rd generation. He was still aware he was at a disadvantage against true Antidiluvians who had millenia of experience on him. Besides the ritual had granted him 3rd generations status for a time, not on a permanent basis. It was at this time that Tremere learned about the continued existence of the Oder of Hermes and by extension of their enemies in the Technocracy. Information that became useful after the Technocracy destroyed Ravnos. Tremere realized the technomages could be used against his other rivals as well, Saulot first among them, and, considering the loss of the compromised Pyramid acceptable, started feeding them information about the prime chantry and defenses.<br /> -Other conspiracies took notice. In the modern nights there was littel doubt the Tremere had become the most powerful clan of them all. This did not sit well with many of the Camarilla vampires. More than a few kindred chafed under the notion the Tremere were so powerful and at the same time so indispensable to the sect. Yet it was undenyable if the Camarilla had resisted the Sabbat in the USA it was mostly due to the resilience of Tremere's chantries that had been able to hold their own even under heavy siege like the one going on for years in New York. Many wished bringing down the warlocks, but doing so could cause the Camarilla itself to collapse. When the Second Inquisition started forming some of these kindred realized it could be used to weaken the Sabbat and then when the opportunity to direct them against the Tremere arose they did nothing to warn the warlocks about what was going to happen. It worked and the Tremere fractured becoming much less powerful inside the Sect. This allowed for more change to be enacted within the Camarilla hierarchy when the Brujah left it killing Hardestadt in the process. The following &quot;regime change&quot; facilitated the further reduction of Tremere political power, as the Camarilla even managed to recruit other blood mages, with a thrid of the Assamites joining and helping establish an effective alliance with the Ashirra to fight the Gehenna Crusade in the Middle East.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T06:57:30-07:00","id":1400952,"title":"","content":"Very good crossover work, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24992\" data-vbnamecard=\"24992\">Haquim</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T04:48:04-07:00","id":1405915,"title":"","content":"I am reviving this topic because now with the Anarch Sourcebook in german it seemed that House Tremere tried to reclaim their control over vienna/tried to dig out some artifacts which whas saw by House Ipssisimus and they sabotaged it.<br /> <br /> Now there are two thinks I wondering.<br /> 1. Whas this before or after Schreckt and the Eldest forbid to get close to Vienna?<br /> 2. How many vampires are still there in Vienna because House Ipssisimus seems to have there some settlement.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T10:41:41-07:00","id":1405961,"title":"","content":"Vampires were probably in Vienna and searching the place for survivors to question and exploit, book, magic items and the like even while the chantry was still burning. Ipssisimus were just the first to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T04:35:08-07:00","id":1406087,"title":"","content":"The Tremere likely took out all the stuff worthwhile before the &quot;bombing&quot; and then added a search after to make it look more legitimate. Much of the stuff left behind for scavengers is either useless or a trap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T05:19:09-07:00","id":1406090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1406087#post1406087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tremere likely took out all the stuff worthwhile before the &quot;bombing&quot; and then added a search after to make it look more legitimate. Much of the stuff left behind for scavengers is either useless or a trap.</div> </div> </div> </div>I unironically love your &quot;this was all a hoax&quot; conspiracy theory. Your commitment to it great.<br /> <br /> :thumbs up:<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T05:45:41-07:00","id":1406100,"title":"","content":"Well, if you thought about it as much as I have, after breaking everything down you'd realise it's the only reasonable, rational explanation apart from 'The Gods went out for a stroll and...' or &quot;bad writers did it&quot;. The former is not particularly interesting to me and tends not to have as much mass appeal and I don't need to explain the latter. The Tremere/Saulot thing isn't particularly attractive from a narrative point of view, nor is it a good justification for the bombing (since there's only so much one can do in Torpor)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T06:52:16-07:00","id":1406103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1406100#post1406100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if you thought about it as much as I have, after breaking everything down you'd realise it's the only reasonable, rational explanation apart from 'The Gods went out for a stroll and...' or &quot;bad writers did it&quot;. The former is not particularly interesting to me and tends not to have as much mass appeal and I don't need to explain the latter. The Tremere/Saulot thing isn't particularly attractive from a narrative point of view, nor is it a good justification for the bombing (since there's only so much one can do in Torpor)</div> </div> </div> </div>Bah, it was all Archmage Tremere wiping out the evil Saulot-Worm thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T07:04:31-07:00","id":1406105,"title":"","content":"But that's really lame.<br /> <br /> Ok, that's like one of those things that sounds really Metal when you describe it the right way but in realistic terms it's the kind of nonsense plot a four year old comes up with when they're playing let's pretend (You can't kill me, I have an invisible shield! I transfered bodies! I Bewitched your servant to bomb your house!)<br /> <br /> I want something more real and tangible that works according to normal conventions of an adult plot. If you're going to do something with such far reaching consequences More Actual-Politics and less a sleeping wizard's 1000 year battle for himself would be ideal; More &quot;As Above, So Below&quot; would fit the Tremere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T16:31:12-07:00","id":1406171,"title":"","content":"They call Saulot &quot;the Dragon&quot;. But they have not said why. I hold that its because he has sown dragons teeth. And that it was time for them to gnaw their way out.<br /> <br /> The ultimate master of Valeren, the discipline of the soul, called to his blood and bid his childer return. And grandchilder, and their childer... every Salubri diablerized by a Tremere, starting to eat their way back up through the souls of the Tremere. Saulot was reclaiming his clan from Tremere. Improved with upgraded Thamaturgy that the Tremere had so obsessively been developing and focusing on for centuries. Really, where did they think that obsession was coming from? And the idea to bond all the young Tremere to their elders... well they mostly ran out of Salubri after a few centuries. There is no Salubri souls in the young Tremere. Once the council of Seven is all Salubri, that was going to be a convenient way to keep the younger ones on a leash. The plans of the Antediluvians are long.<br /> <br /> The destruction of Vienna was Tremeres desperate sacrifice move to keep all the resources out of the hands of his old enemy. Kill all the old Tremere, recreate the clan through the younger ones. Carna, Anarchs etc. Maybe Saulot underestimated the old mages will again. And using the Inquisition against your rivals, letting them kill your childer... that is an old tradition among the kindred. There were very few who could disable ALL the protections and wards of Vienna.<br /> <br /> It is almost funny. &quot;Soul eaters!&quot; was the Tremeres big propaganda push against the Salubri. Saulot must smiled in cold and ancient amusement at that.<br /> <br /> Thats my headcanon of the fall of Vienna, anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T02:13:20-07:00","id":1406237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1406171#post1406171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They call Saulot &quot;the Dragon&quot;. But they have not said why. I hold that its because he has sown dragons teeth. And that it was time for them to gnaw their way out.<br /> <br /> The ultimate master of Valeren, the discipline of the soul, called to his blood and bid his childer return. And grandchilder, and their childer... every Salubri diablerized by a Tremere, starting to eat their way back up through the souls of the Tremere. Saulot was reclaiming his clan from Tremere. Improved with upgraded Thamaturgy that the Tremere had so obsessively been developing and focusing on for centuries. Really, where did they think that obsession was coming from? And the idea to bond all the young Tremere to their elders... well they mostly ran out of Salubri after a few centuries. There is no Salubri souls in the young Tremere. Once the council of Seven is all Salubri, that was going to be a convenient way to keep the younger ones on a leash. The plans of the Antediluvians are long.<br /> <br /> The destruction of Vienna was Tremeres desperate sacrifice move to keep all the resources out of the hands of his old enemy. Kill all the old Tremere, recreate the clan through the younger ones. Carna, Anarchs etc. Maybe Saulot underestimated the old mages will again. And using the Inquisition against your rivals, letting them kill your childer... that is an old tradition among the kindred. There were very few who could disable ALL the protections and wards of Vienna.<br /> <br /> It is almost funny. &quot;Soul eaters!&quot; was the Tremeres big propaganda push against the Salubri. Saulot must smiled in cold and ancient amusement at that.<br /> <br /> Thats my headcanon of the fall of Vienna, anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Iirc that whas one the proposed &quot;canon&quot; stories in BJD too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T06:49:11-07:00","id":1406261,"title":"","content":"Some of that will come down to which version of Saulot was running the Tremere. If it is the hun version, or not-chaotic evil part, then it <i>might </i>involve Saulot bringing back the other Salubri. If it is the p'o version then it won't be calling the Salubri home, except to eat them. Come to that, I've not seen anything that suggests any part of Saulot cared for the Salubri.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T17:45:32-07:00","id":1406354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1406261#post1406261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of that will come down to which version of Saulot was running the Tremere. If it is the hun version, or not-chaotic evil part, then it <i>might </i>involve Saulot bringing back the other Salubri. If it is the p'o version then it won't be calling the Salubri home, except to eat them. Come to that, I've not seen anything that suggests any part of Saulot cared for the Salubri.</div> </div> </div> </div>Time of Thin Blood stated that the true Antediluvians passed Methuselahs thirst ages ago. It implied that can only feed from the fourth and fifth generation. Some night, I suppose even that blood will be too thin...<br /> <br /> But I suspect Saulot has reset the clock a bit on that front. Being in a relatively young body, by Antediluvian standards. Giving Saulot the advantage of being able to be out of torpor and active. Making moves in the world without being at one remove, while the other Antediluvians are sleeping away the eons, waiting for the current crop of blood to thicken and be ready for the harvest.<br /> <br /> But anyway, Saulot was supposed to be fond of Rayzeel. And I think he had an appreciation of his clan as tools. After all, I doubt Samiel got the idea to kick the ass of the Tzimisce Antediluvian on his own. (In as far as It has an ass) Or that Samiel managed to get to a photo finish on his own.<br /> <br /> They're just going to be highly upgraded tools now, with the Thaumaturgy package installed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T18:09:29-07:00","id":1406360,"title":"","content":"The Tzimisce Antediluvian is entirely ass.<br /> <br /> As an aside, my theory is the p'o Saulot is the one Tremere fought, and the one who motivated the Salubri purge. Hun Saulot simply walked away, abandoning the Salubri to their fate, as he went after his own plans for the jyhad.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T19:07:18-07:00","id":1406368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1406354#post1406354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Time of Thin Blood stated that the true Antediluvians passed Methuselahs thirst ages ago. It implied that can only feed from the fourth and fifth generation. Some night, I suppose even that blood will be too thin...</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt it's THAT limiting. There's a wide spectrum of blood concentration between the 5th generation and the 15th, after all. It may be that they get less sustenance from non-elder blood though, and have to resort to diablerie if only thin bloods are available to feed on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T23:08:31-07:00","id":1406388,"title":"","content":"Thoughts? i dislike that happened a lot. Sure mortals can be dangerous to kainites but come on. If THAT was an option the ventrue, lasombra, toreador even tzimisce could have used their mortal connections to pull that off long ago...if mortals are that dangerous, then the lasombra with their church ties could easily wipe out all other clans<br /> <br /> Why havent hunters already wiped out kainites if its that easy? <br /> <br /> Sorry not in my game. Tremere should be the toughest to get rid of kainites out there. Wards, thaumaturgy, planeshifting....a group of dedicated arch mages could do it, but nothing less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T10:15:36-07:00","id":1406803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1406388#post1406388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thoughts? i dislike that happened a lot. Sure mortals can be dangerous to kainites but come on. If THAT was an option the ventrue, lasombra, toreador even tzimisce could have used their mortal connections to pull that off long ago...if mortals are that dangerous, then the lasombra with their church ties could easily wipe out all other clans<br /> <br /> Why havent hunters already wiped out kainites if its that easy?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, but you opened yourself up to this:<br /> <br /> &quot;The Masquerade&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-07-2020, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T10:30:52-07:00","id":1406807,"title":"","content":"Best to worst possibilities<br /> 1- Vienna was an inside job; The Co7 realised the pyramid needed a drastic rebranding to survive the near future, especially with the radical shift in sects from Camarilla to Anarch domination. The split of the house allows for chantries in all sects and reduces the troublesome image of the Tremere being an evil monopoly; It's the perfect move. <br /> 2- The ease of which Vienna was destroyed was exaggerated, it really took a siege to destroy. This works nicely with any other option.<br /> 3- Vienna was due to some BS Saulot/Tremere antideluvian moves that escape the scope of human reason. <br /> 4-Vienna was due to the movements of other methuselah. <br /> 5-This is a case of mistaken identity; a non-SI group took out Vienna. <br /> 6- the SI is the Technocracy (and Vienna might've been given to them by other vampires) <br /> 7- The SI is really that powerful despite being a mortal coalition. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T10:43:07-07:00","id":1406809,"title":"","content":"My inclination is that the Council of Seven was also something that had unwittingly been pushing the power level up of the setting for years. After all, it's seven 4th and 5th generation demigods actively supervising and manipulating the Tremere while also serving as cover for an active 3rd generation Dragon-thing.<br /> <br /> They should have been in torpor by now, all of them, and this was pretty much a way to cut the gordian knot of the Transylvania Chronicles metaplot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T15:30:07-07:00","id":1406846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1406809#post1406809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and this was pretty much a way to cut the gordian knot of the Transylvania Chronicles metaplot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and a useful way to shake things up in general.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T19:45:46-07:00","id":1406884,"title":"","content":"The reason that I'm okay with the destruction of the chantry, besides the obnoxious power creep Phipps mentions, is that if anyone could take them down, it should absolutely be ordinary mortals. Reestablishing that humans are dangerous if they catch on to the existence of Kindred is one of the best things the new edition has done to set a tone apart from the past versions of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T00:20:45-07:00","id":1406912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1406803#post1406803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, but you opened yourself up to this:&quot;The Masquerade&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>i guess ill be banned for arguing with a mod again but you missed my point this was in context<br /> <br /> Are you telling me the lasombra dont have enough chruch ties to inform hunters of where their opponents live? That they Ventrue dont have enough military ties to send the same special forces after their enemies? That the Toreador dont have enough money to hire mercenary troops to achieve the exact same? <br /> We are not talking a small minor chantry full of neonates here. If a hand full of mortals can achieve that, i seriously have to wonder why it was just done in vienna. There may be an answer to this i dont know but....well i seriously dont know. Cause vampires know where their opponents live in many circumstances<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1406884#post1406884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason that I'm okay with the destruction of the chantry, besides the obnoxious power creep Phipps mentions, is that if anyone could take them down, it should absolutely be ordinary mortals. Reestablishing that humans are dangerous if they catch on to the existence of Kindred is one of the best things the new edition has done to set a tone apart from the past versions of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have an issue with it because it was a hand full of mortals. Sure one vampire cant do much against a huge mob. But they have all those disciplines that set them so far apart from any mortal. Tremere in special. Thaumaturgy dammit, celerity, potence, auspex (mind you most tremere begin as ghouls) and ofc they have ghouls - who are also above normal mortals. fortitude and shit.<br /> I am ok with the theme of mortals being a danger to kainites but not in this fashion. Cause it does seem like a fw mortals can easily take out kain himself now. apparently none of the vampiric pros even matter","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T00:32:10-07:00","id":1406913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1406912#post1406912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i guess ill be banned for arguing with a mod again but you missed my point this was in context<br /> <br /> Are you telling me the lasombra dont have enough chruch ties to inform hunters of where their opponents live? That they Ventrue dont have enough military ties to send the same special forces after their enemies? That the Toreador dont have enough money to hire mercenary troops to achieve the exact same?<br /> We are not talking a small minor chantry full of neonates here. If a hand full of mortals can achieve that, i seriously have to wonder why it was just done in vienna. There may be an answer to this i dont know but....well i seriously dont know. Cause vampires know where their opponents live in many circumstances<br /> <br /> <br /> I have an issue with it because it was a hand full of mortals. Sure one vampire cant do much against a huge mob. But they have all those disciplines that set them so far apart from any mortal. Tremere in special. Thaumaturgy dammit, celerity, potence, auspex (mind you most tremere begin as ghouls) and ofc they have ghouls - who are also above normal mortals. fortitude and shit.<br /> I am ok with the theme of mortals being a danger to kainites but not in this fashion. Cause it does seem like a fw mortals can easily take out kain himself now. apparently none of the vampiric pros even matter</div> </div> </div> </div>It's simple. The Lasombra, Ventrue, Toreador etc. did that at one point. It contributed to the first inquisition (And per vampire lore, the vampire side of it was almost entirely because vampires were using mortal proxies to fight their foes). This caused most of vampire society (Including even the sabbat) to adopt the masquerade. As for why they didn't do it to Vienna. Probably because it's the Tremere HQ and it relied upon True Faith hunters and relics. While sending said true faith hunters into an area filled with other occult knowledge and material. Best case that happens with that situation: The hunters kill the Tremere inside, and then they die. Next best case: The hunters die but inflict moderate casualties on the Tremere. The more likely results: The hunters kill the Tremere. And are now equipped with MORE magical artifacts and knowledge. And guess what the person who sent them after is? Or. The hunters die. The Tremere look into who was stupid enough to try that, and kill them.<br /> <br /> Also. Yes. It's Thaumaturgy damn it. It doesn't have a lot of answers to pure mortals. Because pure mortals don't have a lot of things to sympathetically tie to them in hermeticism. And vampires had. Celerity. Potence. Auspex, fortitude, etc. during the middle ages. You know what peasants had back then? Pitchforks and torches. Pitchforks and torches. They still killed A LOT of vampires back then. You know what humans have now? Bombs, night vision goggles, flamethrowers, machine guns, stake launchers. Like. You can disagree that vampires should be threatened by humans. But the lore indicates that humans in enough numbers knowing (And not even that many humans) is a serious threat to vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T01:27:47-07:00","id":1406920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1406913#post1406913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the lore indicates that humans in enough numbers knowing (And not even that many humans) is a serious threat to vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the point i agree with though. In ENOUGH NUMBERS. Not like 5 people taking out the best fortified kainiate stronghold on the planet. As i said a mob with pitchforks and torches can take down a kainite. Sure. But i dont see a specops team taking out the biggest chantry of them all.<br /> Thaumaturgy has answers against pure mortals as well - blood boil, lure of flames etc. that in special lure of flame is more a vampire killer doesnt mean its not also lethal to mortals. cause what kills a vampire in many cases kills a mortal as well<br /> The way this was handled makes mortals look like superior to vampires, as in, on a 1vs1 basis. and that is definitely not the case in the ruleset<br /> i would have appreciated it much more if actual mages say order of hermes took out the vienna chantry. THAT is fine. Heck maybe some werewolves. Something that can deal with magic and kainites. Cause in my oppinion flamethrowers arent enough against kainites with high fortitude, thaumaturgy or say baali. Im also pretty sure some baali were in that chantry as well and they can ignore flamethrowers alltogether","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4364,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","user":"Orkar","date":". 08-08-2020, 04:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T02:54:10-07:00","id":1406926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1406920#post1406920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thaumaturgy has answers against pure mortals as well - blood boil, lure of flames etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>are we talking v5 thaumaturgy or pre-v5 thaumaturgy?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T02:57:51-07:00","id":1406927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1406926#post1406926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> are we talking v5 thaumaturgy or pre-v5 thaumaturgy?</div> </div> </div> </div>my bad i talk pre v5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T03:02:31-07:00","id":1406928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1406927#post1406927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">my bad i talk pre v5.</div> </div> </div> </div>with pre v5 thaum, the co7 would be unbeatable,<br /> even lower ranking wizards with just...transmutation 5 or something, would've made short work of the hunters<br /> <br /> in v5 though...the wizards can still be a challenge, but not an insurmountable one like they used to","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T03:16:22-07:00","id":1406929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1406920#post1406920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is the point i agree with though. In ENOUGH NUMBERS. Not like 5 people taking out the best fortified kainiate stronghold on the planet. As i said a mob with pitchforks and torches can take down a kainite. Sure. But i dont see a specops team taking out the biggest chantry of them all.<br /> Thaumaturgy has answers against pure mortals as well - blood boil, lure of flames etc. that in special lure of flame is more a vampire killer doesnt mean its not also lethal to mortals. cause what kills a vampire in many cases kills a mortal as well<br /> The way this was handled makes mortals look like superior to vampires, as in, on a 1vs1 basis. and that is definitely not the case in the ruleset<br /> i would have appreciated it much more if actual mages say order of hermes took out the vienna chantry. THAT is fine. Heck maybe some werewolves. Something that can deal with magic and kainites. Cause in my oppinion flamethrowers arent enough against kainites with high fortitude, thaumaturgy or say baali. Im also pretty sure some baali were in that chantry as well and they can ignore flamethrowers alltogether</div> </div> </div> </div>I got no problem with what the SI has done, but the speed of their learning curve totally ruins my immersion and breaks suspension of disbelief. Stuff like Karsh should be a massacre, teams of operatives just going dark. Followed by long weeks of forensic analysis on what happened and readjusting assumptions about blankbody abilities. Hell, just running into their first ancilla should be an unexpected, terrifying bloodbath. Theres nowhere near enough working their way up to make it part of a belivable story. The SI accomplishments feel unearned and random.<br /> <br /> Vienna should have involved years of intelligence work first, or been a disaster on an epic (Homeric) scale. And even then, &quot;Success&quot; should not have been total, with off-earth parts holding out.<br /> <br /> It is a recurring problem with the gameline, they build up these terrifying chthonic blood gods, and then make them job, to show that no one is safe. Vitel, Boukephalos, Karsh, Vienna etc.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T04:07:15-07:00","id":1406939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1406929#post1406929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I got no problem with what the SI has done, but the speed of their learning curve totally ruins my immersion and breaks suspension of disbelief. Stuff like Karsh should be a massacre, teams of operatives just going dark. Followed by long weeks of forensic analysis on what happened and readjusting assumptions about blankbody abilities. Hell, just running into their first ancilla should be an unexpected, terrifying bloodbath. Theres nowhere near enough working their way up to make it part of a belivable story. The SI accomplishments feel unearned and random.<br /> <br /> Vienna should have involved years of intelligence work first, or been a disaster on an epic (Homeric) scale. And even then, &quot;Success&quot; should not have been total, with off-earth parts holding out.<br /> <br /> It is a recurring problem with the gameline, they build up these terrifying chthonic blood gods, and then make them job, to show that no one is safe. Vitel, Boukephalos, Karsh, Vienna etc.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well yeah it get even more believable for me, that it whas an inside job, either Tremere wanting free from Saulot, Saulot wanting to cover his tracks, or just generally just playing the weakened headless Clan while in reality it is a grand sheme making everyone trust the Tremere more and let the clan change to see, which ways would strength it most in the long run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T05:23:33-07:00","id":1406952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1406929#post1406929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vienna should have involved years of intelligence work first, or been a disaster on an epic (Homeric) scale. And even then, &quot;Success&quot; should not have been total, with off-earth parts holding out.</div> </div> </div> </div>i like your post. What i want to add: yes mortals have tehcnology that makes them dangerous for vampires. though i see it more as the same way a cow can kill a human as well. Now a major uprising of men against kainites. sure that will end kainites. But while a flamethrower is very dangerous to a kainite...how many stuff ahs the kainite at his disposal thats similarely lethal to the mortal? Specops or not, a bullet in the head will kill you. A vampire? not so much.<br /> <br /> So sure mortals have nightvision googles - ok tremere have auspex that works through walls and warns them ahead of time. And they have wards that do the same and acutally should make evemn entering the chantry a major problem.<br /> Sure mortals have flamethrowers....Tremere have lure of flames.<br /> Sure mortals have guns - so do Tremere.<br /> And id say in the vienna chantry the tremere also had the numbers. And possibly gargoyles who wont give a damn about these weapons the mortals use.<br /> That said the tremere also have a lot of &quot;superior mortals&quot; in ghouls - celerity, potence fortitude...they might be able to take on specops as well.<br /> <br /> In my oppinion .- and its just that im not stating anyrthing here as fact and im not well knowledged about the entire topic to begin with - a reasonable way to get the chantry out would be by employing other supernaturals or the city of vienna uprising against the chantry becasue they found human trafficking, sacrifice or similiar attrocities going on there so you have a literal mob storming the thing. And mind you i expect that more mortals will die than kainites. but the mortals can overwhelm the kainites with numbers. but no mortal should be able to defeat a kainaite in a 1vs1 (except hunters and even they might have their troubles against elders and higher)<br /> <br /> afaik thats the werewolf thing. a fresh werewolf can shred a fresh vampire. a werewolf can tear apart an ancillae. but once a werwolf meets an elder, tables start turning. and with odin (4th gen Gangrel) we have a vampire that hunts Garou for sport. Given what kind of Tremere occupy the vienna chantry those mortals took on several elders. and possibly 4th gens. hows that supposed to happen<br /> <br /> how well trained is a specops with 10 years of training? how well trained is a kainite with 100, 1000 years of training? and thats not even taking into account actual supernatrual traits and disciplines. heck some of those kainaites may have been specops in their mortal lives themselves","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4364,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","user":"Orkar","date":". 08-08-2020, 08:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T07:30:10-07:00","id":1406964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1406912#post1406912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i guess ill be banned for arguing with a mod again but you missed my point this was in context</div> </div> </div> </div>You can argue with me all you want unless it's red text. That's when I'm making official mod decisions.<br /> <br /> And my argument is that if the Masquerade is broken then none of the Elders or their powers will prevent them from getting slaughtered. The Second Inquisition is a danger to all Kindred and perfectly capable of exterminating all vampires everywhere depending on how you want to play them.<br /> <br /> Vienna is to illustrate that people have fucked up enough that no one is safe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1406929#post1406929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I got no problem with what the SI has done, but the speed of their learning curve totally ruins my immersion and breaks suspension of disbelief. Stuff like Karsh should be a massacre, teams of operatives just going dark.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think, canonically, the Second Inquisition DIDN'T kill Karsh but the Camarilla assumes he was killed by them. Karsh was actually killed by Xavier and Theo Bell in the novels. Specifically, he was staked through the heart and dumped in the ocean. If the Second Inquisition did KILL him that would be fishing him out and tossing him in the sun. I assume that Bell wouldn't claim this while he was an Archon.<br /> <br /> Certainly, even BECKETT isn't stupid enough to cop to murdering the Warlord of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> (This happened in the Brujah Trilogy)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-08-2020, 10:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T07:39:59-07:00","id":1406965,"title":"","content":"People tend to have very different ideas of how the Second Inquisition operates and I think the books have contributed to it. My view is the Second Inquisition almost always operates by day, never attempts to &quot;fight&quot; vampires, and when they go after someone who might be awake then they do so with dramatic overreaction. Here is an example of how I imagine vampires are hunted with the successful hunt of a Humanity 0 Nosferatu serial killer in New Jersey.<br /> <br /> You tell me if you don't think its accurate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZUmxYyf_q5k\" data-code=\"ZUmxYyf_q5k\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/ZUmxYyf_q5k/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T08:37:39-07:00","id":1406977,"title":"","content":"I absolutely love the idea of the Second Inquisition. Humans should be more than just food to vampires, and there should be a good reason for the Masquerade. It's accepted in canon that humans were dangerous during the original Inquisition, and that the actions of humanity caused a lot of change to Kindred society, including the formation of the Camarilla, Anarchs, and Sabbat. So why the heck would humanity have gotten less dangerous? There's going to come a tipping point where vampires (or anything else) just cannot hide anymore, at least not as a group. It's going to be up to vampires to manage that as best as they can, because if humanity decides that it's time for vampires to go, the Kindred are done.<br /> <br /> That's my take on it at least. I know that the Tremere are super cool magic badasses (my personal favorite), but they aren't gods, they don't see all, and even super cool magic has limits. One human vs one vamp, probably vamp. A thousand humans vs one vamp, probably humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T08:48:40-07:00","id":1406978,"title":"","content":"My view is the Second Inquisition will die if you get a small group of them alone with you.<br /> <br /> You will die if you try and face them when they're prepared.<br /> <br /> It's really &quot;who attacks first.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T09:04:02-07:00","id":1406980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1406978#post1406978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My view is the Second Inquisition will die if you get a small group of them alone with you.<br /> <br /> You will die if you try and face them when they're prepared.<br /> <br /> It's really &amp;quot;who attacks first.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>As it is with all hunters, however Second Inquisition operatives are a little more bubble wrapped then say Bill, Greg and Steve down at the vfw who are fed up with all the vampires and their lizard people masters ruining their town.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T09:28:50-07:00","id":1406983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChewyGranola</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1406977#post1406977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I absolutely love the idea of the Second Inquisition. Humans should be more than just food to vampires, and there should be a good reason for the Masquerade.</div> </div> </div> </div>the SI isn't a good reason for the masquerade. quite the opposite, they're a good argument against the masquerade, and vampire society is in dire need of a new system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T09:50:47-07:00","id":1406987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1406983#post1406983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the SI isn't a good reason for the masquerade. quite the opposite, they're a good argument against the masquerade, and vampire society is in dire need of a new system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol wut? There is a reason that the first inquisition happened why the traditions got so harshly enforced after the cam was founded. <br /> <br /> Just &quot;coming out of the coffin&quot; won't work in VTM, for every high humanity having kindred you got 5 that are down in the needs to be or already is on a path. Hard to win hearts and minds when there is a couple centuries old guy who wants to turn your family into his living room set because his path tell him to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T09:58:46-07:00","id":1406988,"title":"","content":"<br /> What's more believable:<br /> A: All the secret cabals within various goverments somehow finding eachother and working together, with terrorist groups no less, to fight against vampires. Also the Sabbat have disappeared for unrelated reasons. <br /> <br /> B:The elders, looking to the future, have decided to deal with the severe overpopulation of foolish neonates; They have set up small highly dominated &quot;Inquisition&quot; cells with the information on many neonate havens, and they're going to big up the idea that this is a government action with nothing to do with them and that the surviving neonates should really, really take the masquerade more seriously. Many elders have gone into hiding, and the Sabbat elders, fearing well organized resistance against this plan, have killed off their neonates by murdering them in shipping containers &quot;on route to the Gehenna war&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T10:02:34-07:00","id":1406989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1406987#post1406987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lol wut? There is a reason that the first inquisition happened why the traditions got so harshly enforced after the cam was founded.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, these traditions don't work no more,<br /> the Camarilla went to great lengths to make the masquerade possible,<br /> infiltrating human institutions, seizing the media, supporting pro science paradigms, mind wipes, blood magic etc<br /> <br /> the second inquisition happened anyway,<br /> <br /> either vampires aren't good enough to stay hidden<br /> or humans and technology have evolved enough to render the masquerade pointless or too hard to uphold (they even cracked shrecknet)<br /> or both,<br /> <br /> whatever the case, vampire society can't rely on the masquerade anymore, they're gonna need a better solution for the SI and their successors","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T10:42:08-07:00","id":1406993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1406980#post1406980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As it is with all hunters, however Second Inquisition operatives are a little more bubble wrapped then say Bill, Greg and Steve down at the vfw who are fed up with all the vampires and their lizard people masters ruining their town.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the great equalizer for humanity vs. vampires didn't turn out to be numbers. It turned out to M90s, thermal vision, grenades, and drones. Also the ability to tell police when they show up at a burning house, &quot;Fuck off, I'm with the government.&quot;<br /> <br /> Mind you, I actually said the great equalizer for the Anarchs vs. Elders was the invention of automatic weapons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1406988#post1406988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's more believable:<br /> A: All the secret cabals within various goverments somehow finding each other and working together, with terrorist groups no less, to fight against vampires. Also the Sabbat have disappeared for unrelated reasons.<br /> <br /> B:The elders, looking to the future, have decided to deal with the severe overpopulation of foolish neonates; They have set up small highly dominated &quot;Inquisition&quot; cells with the information on many neonate havens, and they're going to big up the idea that this is a government action with nothing to do with them and that the surviving neonates should really, really take the masquerade more seriously. Many elders have gone into hiding, and the Sabbat elders, fearing well organized resistance against this plan, have killed off their neonates by murdering them in shipping containers &quot;on route to the Gehenna war&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>A.<br /> <br /> If one secret government agency finds out about vampires, you better damn believe most will.<br /> <br /> Mind you, Elders are petty assholes in my view and that they're almost certainly likely to support the Inquisition against each other than work with against it together. Mind you, I also believe that the Second Inquisition has reached the limit of its accomplishments too. The World of Darkness is so cynical and so horrifying that after hunting a bunch of vampires for a few years, I fully believe the world governments will eventually give up and declare victory.<br /> <br /> Which I think they objectively stated was what they did in THE CAMARILLA after Vienna.<br /> <br /> We're now in &quot;mop up&quot; mode.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1406989#post1406989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> yeah, these traditions don't work no more,<br /> the Camarilla went to great lengths to make the masquerade possible,<br /> infiltrating human institutions, seizing the media, supporting pro science paradigms, mind wipes, blood magic etc<br /> <br /> the second inquisition happened anyway,</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Sabbat flat out didn't bother with it and eventually the Camarilla tried to manipulate the government against them. Whoever did that is a moron and ruined everything.<br /> <br /> But if only 2/3rds of Vampiredom is practicing the Masquerade, the situation is fucked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-08-2020, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T11:19:09-07:00","id":1406999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1406993#post1406993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the Sabbat flat out didn't bother with it and eventually the Camarilla tried to manipulate the government against them. Whoever did that is a moron and ruined everything.<br /> <br /> But if only 2/3rds of Vampiredom is practicing the Masquerade, the situation is fucked.</div> </div> </div> </div>2/3rds? 2/3RDS? what 2/3rds?<br /> <br /> only a minority of the society (elders) can uphold the Masquerade,<br /> everyone else is a breach waiting to happen<br /> <br /> that's one reason the sabbat has the elders handle the breaches, and don't enforce the masquerade on the youngsters: cause the younsters can't!<br /> <br /> and now in v5, even the elders can't (Vienna)<br /> <br /> you know, that 1/3rd of vampiredom was right about one thing: only Caine can save vampiredom, and he ain't showing up<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T11:22:10-07:00","id":1407000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1406999#post1406999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2/3rds? 2/3RDS? what 2/3rds?<br /> <br /> only a minority of the society (elders) can uphold the Masquerade,<br /> everyone else is a breach waiting to happen<br /> <br /> that's one reason the sabbat has the elders handle the breaches, and don't enforce the masquerade on the youngsters: cause the younsters can't!<br /> <br /> and now in v5, even the elders can't (Vienna)<br /> <br /> you know, that 1/3rd of vampiredom was right about one thing: only Caine can save vampiredom, and he ain't showing up</div> </div> </div> </div>Sabbat/Anarchs/Camarilla<br /> <br /> 1/3rd being the Sabbat<br /> <br /> The Sabbat did not give sufficient attention the Masquerade unlike everyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T11:48:53-07:00","id":1407005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1407000#post1407000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sabbat/Anarchs/Camarilla<br /> <br /> 1/3rd being the Sabbat<br /> <br /> The Sabbat did not give sufficient attention the Masquerade unlike everyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah,<br /> vampires on paths of enlightenment who didn't have to worry about how many witnesses they eliminated/memory wiped/replaced with fleshcrafted clones,<br /> vampires that held smaller herds and ghouls, and had less contact with mortal institutions (most of which were gatekept by the Ventrue anyway),<br /> vampires who had &quot;elders&quot; and select bishoprics taking on the job of keeping the silence of the blood<br /> somehow isn't &quot;sufficient&quot;<br /> <br /> tell me, what IS sufficient?<br /> <br /> I'm telling you what is sufficient: vampires stop being vampires, that's what's sufficient nowadays, and that's what v5's selling us, a vampire game about not being a vampire","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T12:07:21-07:00","id":1407007,"title":"","content":"The Sabbat for all they supposedly thumbed their nose at the Masquerade, did enforce it in their own way. They called it &quot;Don't shit where you eat&quot;. It's talked about in the Revised Sabbat Book. The Elders of the Sabbat looked at it as common sense to not let the Mortals know about them... But then, as it's pointed out with the Sabbat Vampires... when someone see's Obtenbration or Visccitude they don't think &quot;Vampire&quot;, they think something like &quot;Demon&quot;, and the Sabbat was fine with that too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T12:28:18-07:00","id":1407014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1407005#post1407005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> yeah,<br /> vampires on paths of enlightenment who didn't have to worry about how many witnesses they eliminated/memory wiped/replaced with fleshcrafted clones,<br /> vampires that held smaller herds and ghouls, and had less contact with mortal institutions (most of which were gatekept by the Ventrue anyway),<br /> vampires who had &quot;elders&quot; and select bishoprics taking on the job of keeping the silence of the blood<br /> somehow isn't &quot;sufficient&quot;<br /> <br /> tell me, what IS sufficient?<br /> <br /> I'm telling you what is sufficient: vampires stop being vampires, that's what's sufficient nowadays, and that's what v5's selling us, a vampire game about not being a vampire</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree. In our MTA Round the Tremere True Love of my character obfuscate as the Daughter and later Granddaughter of herself that whas rescued by her future &quot;husband&quot; (her sire that raised her from the dead) during the Reichskristallnacht. With the first two Dots of Viscittude she stole from a Tzimisce, she changed slightly the look of herself and her sire to make herself look different and masquerade as different generations. She survived Vienna because she got right to have a haven outside of the chantry and whas able with her charade to have believable bank accounts that did not looked like a vampires but one of wealthy family.<br /> <br /> After Vienna she survived by avoiding feeding from humans but got her blood created from her TL via Magick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":26160,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","user":"Koronus","date":". 08-08-2020, 08:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T13:12:47-07:00","id":1407022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1406993#post1406993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If one secret government agency finds out about vampires, you better damn believe most will.</div> </div> </div> </div>And how exactly do these secret goverment agencies find out about other secret goverment agencies? If they're not that secret, how come the vampires didn't find them then? You don't think the vampires have got eyes here watching for that kind of stuff? <br /> <br /> Look, I know you really like this idea, but it's not a good one. Take a step back and really look at things: <br /> A Small group of goverment agents interested in vampires can stay secret, but can't do any damage. <br /> A collection of government agents large enough to do international damage, and interested in doing so, cannot stay secret, and thus cannot do serious damage before it's too late. <br /> <br /> There are two exceptions <br /> 1- The masquerade is completely blown off all of these agents decide it's time to leak as much information as possible to the guys with the willingness and tools to do something before the vampires can muster an effective counter. of course militaries and law enforcement will probably need a few days to actually work out what to do, giving vampires the vital time to prepare whilst the military/LE await the inevitable 'do nothing' order by politicians, if not a &quot;control the population&quot; order but... I'm sure that information will get to some people who do wanna kill vampires real bad. <br /> <br /> 2- The SI is really just an elder conspiracy against the young. <br /> <br /> As the first option hasn't happened, the only reasonable option is number 2. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T13:55:01-07:00","id":1407025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1407022#post1407022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how exactly do these secret goverment agencies find out about other secret goverment agencies? If they're not that secret, how come the vampires didn't find them then? You don't think the vampires have got eyes here watching for that kind of stuff?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it's stated that it was the Camarilla who actually caused these people to find out about these things because they were the ones who showed them the Sabbat and Anarchs because they believed they could use the United States military (and other groups) as weapons. This backfired and resulted in them spreading information and working to undermine their agents or free them until it was uncontrollable.<br /> <br /> The governments are keeping it to themselves but I'm easily of the mind that the Elders can fuck up this badly and their response is to blame the Anarchs for it.<br /> <br /> But here's the thing, a lot of this is up to the ST's interpretation. I actually don't think it has to be one way or another ans think it'd be a mistake for White Wolf to state it's absolutely one thing.<br /> <br /> Your version of what's &quot;really&quot; going on is just as much valid as mine and vice versa. I think you need some flexibility given how everyone treats Elders and NPCs differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T14:18:53-07:00","id":1407028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1407025#post1407025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe it's stated that it was the Camarilla who actually caused these people to find out about these things because they were the ones who showed them the Sabbat and Anarchs because they believed they could use the United States military (and other groups) as weapons. This backfired and resulted in them spreading information and working to undermine their agents or free them until it was uncontrollable..</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a... not a great excuse. Imagine you wanted to kill a specific child for whatever reason (I dunno... you think he wants to eat you?) Do you use your hands, a blade, a handgun, an attack dog, a fire, an IED, set your own kid against him, or get the military to carpetbomb his entire district?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T14:27:41-07:00","id":1407030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1407028#post1407028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a... not a great excuse. Imagine you wanted to kill a specific child for whatever reason (I dunno... you think he wants to eat you?) Do you use your hands, a blade, a handgun, an attack dog, a fire, an IED, set your own kid against him, or get the military to carpetbomb his entire district?</div> </div> </div> </div>Alas, Elders just didn't know what they were playing with.<br /> <br /> Mind you, one criticism I do have of the Second Inquisition is the fact it's just a Greatest Hits version of the original.<br /> <br /> * The Lasombra and Goratrix use the Catholic Church against the Templars. It is wildly successful.<br /> * The Lasombra then use it against fellow vampires.<br /> * The Inquisition notices the Lasombra are vampires.<br /> * The Inquisition spirals out of control<br /> * The Elders blame the Neonates and abridge any responsibility.<br /> * The Elders toss their children at the Inquisition, making it even more successful.<br /> * The Anarch Revolt happens.<br /> * Having nothing left to lose the Anarchs make a deal with a Independent Clan and become their own sect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T14:30:59-07:00","id":1407031,"title":"","content":"As far as that last bit, I could see an argument for it representing the cyclical nature of time or the sins of the father repeating upon the son or even just history repeating itself.<br /> <br /> Of course the answer might also well be just a shrug and \u201ccan\u2019t beat the classics\u201d, which wouldn\u2019t bother me either. Heck, I like a bit of tongue and cheek here and there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T17:16:12-07:00","id":1407050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1407030#post1407030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alas, Elders just didn't know what they were playing with.<br /> <br /> Mind you, one criticism I do have of the Second Inquisition is the fact it's just a Greatest Hits version of the original.<br /> <br /> * The Lasombra and Goratrix use the Catholic Church against the Templars. It is wildly successful.<br /> * The Lasombra then use it against fellow vampires.<br /> * The Inquisition notices the Lasombra are vampires.<br /> * The Inquisition spirals out of control<br /> * The Elders blame the Neonates and abridge any responsibility.<br /> * The Elders toss their children at the Inquisition, making it even more successful.<br /> * The Anarch Revolt happens.<br /> * Having nothing left to lose the Anarchs make a deal with a Independent Clan and become their own sect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Question. Lore of the Clans make the Toreador claim they are responsible for First Inquisition because they believed if the church would be busy with a chism they would not reconize the vampires but it spiraled out of control because they saw to late how the Inquisition got the dominating faction.<br /> How is this fitting in in the first Inquisition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T19:08:53-07:00","id":1407064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1407050#post1407050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Question. Lore of the Clans make the Toreador claim they are responsible for First Inquisition because they believed if the church would be busy with a chism they would not reconize the vampires but it spiraled out of control because they saw to late how the Inquisition got the dominating faction.<br /> How is this fitting in in the first Inquisition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just about everyone has a story claiming the Inquisition was their &quot;fault&quot; with the Setites claiming it was their revenge on Europe for example. I'm inclined to think just about every vampire Clan had SOMEONE really screwing up things.<br /> <br /> Let's face it, the Omen War is pretty much proof positive that Satan's forces were at work. Maybe you shouldn't make armies of flesh-monsters and gargoyles, you two.<br /> <br /> Rafaele de Corazon was correct that EVERYONE was acting overt because they didn't think humans were capable of striking back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T19:52:09-07:00","id":1407068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1407064#post1407064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rafaele de Corazon was correct that EVERYONE was acting overt because they didn't think humans were capable of striking back.</div> </div> </div> </div>And history doesn't so much repeat, as rhyme.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T20:20:23-07:00","id":1407071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1407068#post1407068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And history doesn't so much repeat, as rhyme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind you, it's a double irony with Rafaele because his backstory is that his Toreador sire brought an enormous harem/herd with her as well as enough money to fund the Reconquista to visit with a Bishop when he met her.<br /> <br /> Vampires were living large back then.<br /> <br /> I also love that his forwarding of the Masquerade was because he basically picked a Bible verse from the Book of Nod at random to try to get some attention. It worked, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T23:06:05-07:00","id":1407093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1407064#post1407064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just about everyone has a story claiming the Inquisition was their &amp;quot;fault&amp;quot; with the Setites claiming it was their revenge on Europe for example. I'm inclined to think just about every vampire Clan had SOMEONE really screwing up things.</div> </div> </div> </div>^This, and consider that characters don't have the game book collections that we do. Every vampire old enough to remember those nights is aware of their own attempts to weaponize the Church, but may or may not know the full extent of what their rivals were up to. Like a version of the Tragedy of the Commons, except every individual is winding up the same murder machine instead of drawing too much from the village well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T02:19:50-07:00","id":1407106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1407030#post1407030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alas, Elders just didn't know what they were playing with.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div> Huge government agencies are generally things you actually have to learn about before you can incorperate them into your scheme. Unlike the catholic church, They aren't using easily accessible buildings that stand out, government agents aren't lying around on the street during the nighttime with advertisements of what they do. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T04:48:23-07:00","id":1407117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1407106#post1407106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huge government agencies are generally things you actually have to learn about before you can incorperate them into your scheme. Unlike the catholic church, They aren't using easily accessible buildings that stand out, government agents aren't lying around on the street during the nighttime with advertisements of what they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually what went wrong, My Wife is Scary because what fucked up the Camarilla with the NSA isn't a nebulous &quot;thing that went wrong.&quot; It was specifically that they did most of their business with Felicity Price [a character from the original HUNTER'S HUNTED] and a Deputy Director of the organization. She was Dominated into being the Camarilla's primary agent in the organization and eventually threw it off before contacting all the other supernatural believers in the group [there were a lot due to the Chaosscopes] and telling them everything she knew.<br /> <br /> Mind you, the NSA's lunatics are why they believe vampires are other dimensional parasites. Since they have things that can see the Underworld and spirits--and assume the two are related.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T04:58:29-07:00","id":1407120,"title":"","content":"...and that isn't contrived stupidity... how?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T05:19:57-07:00","id":1407122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1407120#post1407120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and that isn't contrived stupidity... how?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because of course an Elder is going to dominate someone that is an expert in the field veruss try to control it directly? Duh. You're not going to learn Computer 5 to take over Silicone Valley, you're going to Dominate Peter Thiel into doing what you need for him.<br /> <br /> That's just basic common sense. By the time an Elder mastered it, technology would have changed and the NSA is based on being at the forerfront of technology.<br /> <br /> You use moles and ghouls for a reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T08:56:32-07:00","id":1407145,"title":"","content":"But they aren't though. Dominate is for rookies and contingencies. any elder worth their salt is going to win such people over with a friendship of wealth and benefits. perhaps blackmail or threats, but you dont put all your hopes into a magical power. That's a rookie mistake, and elders by definition aren't rookies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T10:56:49-07:00","id":1407157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1407145#post1407145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But they aren't though. Dominate is for rookies and contingencies. any elder worth their salt is going to win such people over with a friendship of wealth and benefits. perhaps blackmail or threats, but you dont put all your hopes into a magical power. That's a rookie mistake, and elders by definition aren't rookies.</div> </div> </div> </div>No Elder would reward cattle.<br /> <br /> The idea of <i>speaking </i>with Kine that aren't ghouls is difficult to fathom.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs are the fools that believe humans actually have feelings or thoughts.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T10:58:44-07:00","id":1407158,"title":"","content":"Do you have a more serious argument?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T11:19:10-07:00","id":1407161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1407157#post1407157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No Elder would reward cattle.<br /> <br /> The idea of <i>speaking </i>with Kine that aren't ghouls is difficult to fathom.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs are the fools that believe humans actually have feelings or thoughts.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>This has been the expressed position of the entire Sabbat for ages, and the tacit opinion of most Camarilla elders for ages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T11:19:20-07:00","id":1407162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1407158#post1407158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have a more serious argument?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm saying that your opinion of Elders devoting this much time to their relationships is not something that reflects what we've seen in the books. A lot of Camarilla Elders and Ventrue in particular use Dominate so they DON'T have traceable relationships to people.<br /> <br /> Mind you, the thing worked for TWENTY YEARS without a hitch.<br /> <br /> It just failed because her conditioning broke.<br /> <br /> Possibly because the Elder was killed or Beckoned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T11:45:36-07:00","id":1407164,"title":"","content":"You don't need to build wonderful relationships with people, you need groups that represent you to represent your interests to people you want to influence.... and the ventrue scorn a reliance on Disciplines (LotC at least) to get what mundane persuasion should. (and you're no doubt going to have friends and rivals meeting with the person's peers and subordinates) and if the person does start acting against that thing that's controlled them for years... well they aren't going to be around for long are they? <br /> <br /> It's a farce. <br /> <br /> Only believable option is that this FP didn't break her Dominate, the Dominate changed, and so did the dominates of those in proximity...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T11:57:06-07:00","id":1407167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1407164#post1407164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't need to build wonderful relationships with people, you need groups that represent you to represent your interests to people you want to influence.... and the ventrue scorn a reliance on Disciplines (LotC at least) to get what mundane persuasion should. (and you're no doubt going to have friends and rivals meeting with the person's peers and subordinates) and if the person does start acting against that thing that's controlled them for years... well they aren't going to be around for long are they?<br /> <br /> It's a farce.<br /> <br /> Only believable option is that this FP didn't break her Dominate, the Dominate changed, and so did the dominates of those in proximity...</div> </div> </div> </div>Or he got killed and all of his people immediately snapped free.<br /> <br /> Just saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T12:15:52-07:00","id":1407168,"title":"","content":"and everyone else who had an interest in that area? Nobody stepped up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T14:25:15-07:00","id":1407183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1407168#post1407168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and everyone else who had an interest in that area? Nobody stepped up?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, vampires haven't been exterminated, so yes, someone obviously did.<br /> <br /> It's just that maybe the world's greatest strategists, technologists, and spies are not something the Camarilla can just wave their hand and make go away.<br /> <br /> Especially during a massive political and social upheaval with the Beckoning and Third Anarch Revolt.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla is not rolling over for the Second Inquisition but its a fight against a foe that is every bit capable of destroying them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T19:32:47-07:00","id":1407422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1331291#post1331291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well the issue is that their goals are:<br /> <br /> Camarilla: To survive<br /> Technocracy: To destroy all supernaturals<br /> <br /> They can work together but the thing is that the Technocracy feels the same way about vampires that Lupines do. They consider vampires everything wrong with the world and proof positive what they're doing is right.<br /> <br /> And maybe, with vampires, they're right.</div> </div> </div> </div>You clearly don't know enough about the Technocracy. Their goal isn't to destroy supernaturals. Their goal is to guide humanity towards their vision of enlightenment. This takes place by reinforcing (controlling) sleepers beliefs in the Consensus. Their biggest threats are things that openly challenge the status quo, not things that reinforce it like vamps tend to do. Sure eventually Vamps need to go, but after the things that threaten the Consensus in more direct ways. The fact that vamps hide themselves and police that policy means that the Technocracy doesn't have to spend it's own resources to cover for them.<br /> <br /> Also T20 view seems to be DO NOT kill Vamps as the blowback tends not to be worth the resources involved. (page 7 manuscript preview 2)<br /> <br /> Also if it were that Easy to take down vampire strong holds with mortals why didn't the Order of Hermes use that tactic? The are not bound by the masquerade. And thanks to Tremere rituals, there is no such thing as walking into the chantry during the day. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25664-gubenyochi","name":"Gubenyochi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T19:37:09-07:00","id":1407424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gubenyochi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1330022-v5-thoughts-on-vienna?p=1407422#post1407422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You clearly don't know enough about the Technocracy. Their goal isn't to destroy supernaturals. Their goal is to guide humanity towards their vision of enlightenment. This takes place by reinforcing (controlling) sleepers beliefs in the Consensus. Their biggest threats are things that openly challenge the status quo, not things that reinforce it like vamps tend to do. Sure eventually Vamps need to go, but after the things that threaten the Consensus in more direct ways. The fact that vamps hide themselves and police that policy means that the Technocracy doesn't have to spend it's own resources to cover for them.<br /> <br /> Also T20 view seems to be DO NOT kill Vamps as the blowback tends not to be worth the resources involved. (page 7 manuscript preview 2)<br /> <br /> Also if it were that Easy to take down vampire strong holds with mortals why didn't the Order of Hermes use that tactic? The are not bound by the masquerade. And thanks to Tremere rituals, there is no such thing as walking into the chantry during the day. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>*cough* Pogrom *cough*<br /> <br /> The T20 also doesn't count because that book is explictly how the Technocracy has changed virtually every single operating procedure for the 21st century.<br /> <br /> And the Order of Hermes DID take out a bunch of them. There was a huge massive war....that occupied one book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>